    description: "F62.A3 (blind severity 3/Moderate; F74.A2 placeholder-counting-convention EXTENSION folded here). A reasonable consumer reads is_resolved=False as 'the dst symbol does not exist in the graph.' Empirically 100% of the 24244 is_resolved=False edges point at a dst that DOES exist — every one an external_symbol-kind placeholder node — and 0 edges have is_resolved=True with a missing dst. So is_resolved is orthogonal to dst-node existence; its true meaning is 'the dst is a synthetic external placeholder, not a real in-repo symbol' — a meaning the docstring ('dst symbol was resolved at analysis time') leaves ambiguous. The graph is referentially complete (no dangling dst) but the flag is overloaded. A graph-traversal consumer that special-cases 'if not edge.is_resolved: skip # dst wont be in graph' wrongly skips edges whose dst IS a (placeholder) node. Fix: document that an unresolved edge still has a materialized placeholder node (present-but-synthetic, not absent). filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # eb88
